ln - make a link

SYNOPSIS
    ln -s TARGET NAME

DESCRIPTION
    Makes NAME a symbolic link holding the text TARGET.

    Only symbolic links. A hard link is a second directory entry for one
    inode, which the filesystem underneath could do, but the two are not
    variations of one idea and offering ln without -s when only -s works
    would be worse than offering neither.

    The target is stored as written and is not checked. A link to something
    that does not exist is a normal thing to have.

SEE ALSO
    readlink, ls, rm
